From a507c2b2dbaf42534d75d486c1835a53eccbd367 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:20:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 177/240] Bugfix: convert MeTiS v5 partitioning parameters into
 Scotch ones [report R. Perry]

The MeTiS v5 partitioning routines passed the `ubvec` array, which
holds imbalance ratios greater than one (e.g. 1.05), as the Scotch
imbalance tolerance (e.g. 0.05), so that a 5% tolerance resulted in
partitions with parts of twice the average load. In the recursive
routine, a NULL `ubvec` was dereferenced. With `ncon` greater than
one, the interleaved vertex weight array was read as one weight per
vertex.

Both v5 routines now share `_SCOTCH_METIS_V5_PartGraph()`, which checks
and converts the parameters: `ubvec[0]` is turned into a tolerance, a
NULL `ubvec` yields the default tolerance, and the first vertex
constraint is gathered into a temporary array, as was already done for
target part weights. `ParMETIS_V3_PartKway()` receives the same
treatment: `ubvec[0]` is used to build the mapping strategy, and the
vertex and part weights of the first constraint are gathered with the
proper stride.

Refs: CLI-02, CLI-03, CLI-07
